    {
      "pattern": "Adjective + 一点儿 (a bit more)",
      "explanation_en": "Put 一点儿 after an adjective to say something is a little more than something else, often used in comparing.",
      "example_zh": "今天比昨天冷一点儿。",
      "example_en": "Today is a bit colder than yesterday."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "应该 + verb (should)",
      "explanation_en": "应该 goes before a verb to say what someone should do. Adding 呢 to a question makes it sound like you are thinking it over.",
      "example_zh": "我应该去哪儿吃饭呢？",
